cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use biosim-lab in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "biosim-lab: an open-source, plugin-based virtual laboratory instrument platform"
abstract: >-
  biosim-lab simulates the analyses performed by commercial bio-instruments —
  impedance-based real-time cell analysis, standing-surface-acoustic-wave cell
  sorting, automated cell counting and live-cell tracking — using only free and
  open-source Python tooling, and runs the same analyses on measured instrument
  data. Every physical constant carries either a DOI or an explicit ASSUMPTION
  label, and heavy external solvers (OpenFOAM, Elmer) are optional plugins that
  the core works completely without.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/biosim-lab/biosim-lab"
keywords:
  - acoustofluidics
  - microfluidics
  - finite element method
  - circulating tumor cells
  - impedance spectroscopy
  - cell tracking
  - open source
authors:
